  "guidebook": {
    "intro": "Kiingereza kina njia mbili za kawaida za wakati uliopita: **have + kitenzi** (kama **-me-**) na wakati uliopita sahili (kama **-li-**).",
    "phrases": [
      { "target": "Have you eaten?", "base": "Umekula?" },
      { "target": "I’ve already eaten.", "base": "Tayari nimekula." },
      { "target": "I haven’t eaten yet.", "base": "Bado sijala." },
      { "target": "What did you do yesterday?", "base": "Ulifanya nini jana?" },
      { "target": "Yesterday I went to the market.", "base": "Jana nilienda sokoni." },
      { "target": "Last year we went to Zanzibar.", "base": "Mwaka jana tulienda Zanzibar." }
    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "present-perfect",
        "title": "-me-: I have…",
        "body": [
          "**-me-** ya Kiswahili mara nyingi ni **have/has** + kitenzi cha tatu: **nimekula → I have eaten (I’ve eaten)**, **nimemaliza → I’ve finished**.",
          "Kukanusha: **I haven’t eaten** (sijala). **Already** (tayari) na **yet** (bado) hukaa na wakati huu: **I haven’t eaten yet.**"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "past-simple",
        "title": "-li-: wakati uliopita",
        "body": [
          "Vitenzi vingi huongeza **-ed**: **walk → walked**, **arrive → arrived**. Kitenzi hakibadiliki kwa mtu: **I/you/she/we/they walked**.",
          "Vitenzi vya kawaida sana havina kanuni, vikariri: **go → went**, **eat → ate**, **do → did**, **buy → bought**, **see → saw**."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Last week",
        "body": [
          "Maneno ya wakati uliopita: **yesterday** (jana), **the day before yesterday** (juzi), **last week** (wiki iliyopita), **last year** (mwaka jana). Huja mwanzoni au mwishoni: **Last year I went to Zanzibar.**"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
